WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.687
On this slide, we are focusing on distribution with bins.

00:00:03.687 --> 00:00:08.242
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.242 --> 00:00:16.742
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:16.742 --> 00:00:21.962
A distribution shows how values are spread across ranges and can reveal concentration, skew, gaps,

00:00:21.962 --> 00:00:28.692
or unusual observations. Before clicking Run, predict the statistic or pattern you expect.

00:00:28.692 --> 00:00:32.497
After it runs, interpret the result in words.

00:00:32.497 --> 00:00:36.947
Then change one value and see whether the interpretation changes.

00:00:36.947 --> 00:00:41.157
Focus on meaning and limitations, not only the calculation.

00:00:41.157 --> 00:00:46.902
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:46.902 --> 00:00:52.318
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
